import ../../../testing/driver.dl
import ../../../ui/choice_popovers.dl

document example:
    text surface "Source" containing "hello" using no UI appearance

to get [read test choices] {a pointer:context} [in] {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    set popup to context as a pointer to UI choice popover
    set result to read UI choice popover popup in view
    return result != 0

set instance to an instance of example
set window to the address of instance
set view to a UI view of window sized 900 by 600 using font "regular" with the test UI driver
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
queue UI input of kind 3 key 258 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
set source to view's selection's caret source
set caret to view's selection's caret
set popup to a UI choice popover
set other to a UI choice popover
set transform to @intrinsic("construct", UI transform, 0.0, -2.0, 3.0, 0.0, 100.0, 50.0)
set rotated to UI bounds (UI box at 10 20 sized 5 7) transformed by transform
require condition (((rotated's x = 46.0) and (rotated's y = 80.0)) and ((rotated's width = 14.0) and (rotated's height = 15.0))) reporting "A transformed anchor lost its enclosing bounds."
add UI choice "independent" enabled true to (the address of other)
add UI choice "unavailable" enabled false to (the address of popup)
set index to 0
loop while index < 12:
    add UI choice ("option " + (the string form of index)) enabled (index != 2) to (the address of popup)
    increment index
show UI choice popover (the address of popup) reporting "" with hint "Enter choose · Esc close" in (the address of view)
set layout to the UI layout for element (the control labeled "Source" in window) in (view's layout)
set frame to @intrinsic("construct", UI frame, the address of view, true)
paint UI choice popover (the address of popup) anchored at (UI box at 880 574 sized 1 12) within (UI box at 0 0 sized 900 600) using (layout's typeface) styled (layout's appearance) on frame
require condition ((popup's rows = 8) and (popup's selected = 1)) reporting "Choice lists did not skip an unavailable first item."
require condition ((popup's bounds' x >= 8.0) and ((popup's bounds' x + popup's bounds' width) <= 892.0)) reporting "Choices extended outside their viewport."
require condition ((popup's bounds' y >= 8.0) and ((popup's bounds' y + popup's bounds' height) <= 592.0)) reporting "Choices extended below their viewport."
set overlay to a UI overlay in (the address of view) with context ((the address of popup) as a pointer) handling input ((the function named "read test choices $ in $") as a pointer) painting (0 as a pointer) closing (0 as a pointer)
set overlay's layout to the address of (popup's surface)
queue UI input of kind 3 key 264 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
process UI input in (the address of view)
require condition (popup's selected = 2) reporting "Arrow navigation did not select the next choice."
queue UI input of kind 3 key 264 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
process UI input in (the address of view)
require condition (popup's selected = 4) reporting "Arrow navigation selected a disabled choice."
queue UI input of kind 3 key 269 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
process UI input in (the address of view)
require condition (popup's selected = 12) reporting "End did not select the final choice."
paint UI choice popover (the address of popup) anchored at (UI box at 880 574 sized 1 12) within (UI box at 0 0 sized 900 600) using (layout's typeface) styled (layout's appearance) on frame
require condition (popup's first = 5) reporting "The selected choice did not scroll into view."
queue UI input of kind 3 key 264 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
process UI input in (the address of view)
require condition (popup's selected = 1) reporting "Arrow navigation did not wrap past disabled choices."
require condition ((view's selection's caret source = source) and (view's selection's caret = caret)) reporting "Choosing an item stole the editor caret."
require condition (other's selected = 0) reporting "Choice lists shared selection state."
set view's cursor shape to 2
queue UI input of kind 1 key 0 at (popup's bounds' x + 2.0) (popup's bounds' y + 2.0) with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
process UI input in (the address of view)
require condition (view's cursor shape = 0) reporting "Choice padding retained the editor's text cursor."
set view's key press to 257
require condition ((read UI choice popover (the address of popup) in (the address of view)) = 2) reporting "Enter did not activate the selected choice."
set view's key press to 256
require condition ((read UI choice popover (the address of popup) in (the address of view)) = 3) reporting "Escape did not request dismissal."
paint UI choice popover (the address of popup) anchored at (UI box at 0 0 sized 1 12) within (UI box at 0 0 sized 20 20) using (layout's typeface) styled (layout's appearance) on frame
set view's key press to 257
require condition ((read UI choice popover (the address of popup) in (the address of view)) != 2) reporting "An invisible choice list activated an item."
dismiss UI choice popover (the address of popup) in (the address of view)
require condition ((popup's surface's hit bounds' width = 0.0) and (popup's rows = 0)) reporting "A dismissed choice list retained input geometry."
detach UI overlay overlay in (the address of view)
clear UI choice popover (the address of popup) in (the address of view)
add UI choice "disabled" enabled false to (the address of popup)
show UI choice popover (the address of popup) reporting "" with hint "Esc close" in (the address of view)
paint UI choice popover (the address of popup) anchored at (UI box at 0 0 sized 1 12) within (UI box at 0 0 sized 900 600) using (layout's typeface) styled (layout's appearance) on frame
set view's key press to 269
ignore read UI choice popover (the address of popup) in (the address of view)
set view's key press to 257
require condition ((read UI choice popover (the address of popup) in (the address of view)) != 2) reporting "An entirely disabled list activated a choice."
clear UI choice popover (the address of popup) in (the address of view)
clear UI choice popover (the address of other) in (the address of view)
close the address of view
close window
print line "Choice popovers share bounded rendering, disabled rows, scrolling and keyboard capture without changing editor focus."
